+      "generation_rule": "push_generation is a rank-local u32[2] (zero-initialized once with the flags): [0] counts the completed forwards of this rank, [1] is the local_pack CTA arrival counter.  publish_push reads [0] = g and stores g + 1 into push_flags[this_rank][token] of every destination rank after its inbox pushes completed; local_pack CTA (src, token) reads [0] = g, waits until its LOCAL push_flags[src][token] == g + 1, and the last CTA of the grid ([1] reaches gridDim.x) stores [1] = 0 and [0] = g + 1.  Flags are never reset, so a slot that is not pushed in a forward (token >= tokens_per_rank, or a shrunken token count) keeps an older value that never equals the expected generation; every rank must execute the same number of forwards (eager prewarm before capture, then graph replays), exactly as the pull route's barriers required.",
+      "push_rule": "for every destination rank d < world: if any of the token's 8 expert ids has owner id // 32 == d, one cp.async.bulk of the whole 3232-byte slot; else one 64-byte cp.async.bulk of the ids+weights tail only (so the destination can see that none of the routes is its own); then cp.async.bulk.commit_group, cp.async.bulk.wait_group 0, fence.proxy.async.global, fence.release.sys and one st.relaxed.sys.u32 of g + 1 into each destination's flag.  Masked ids (< 0 or >= 512) select no destination.",
