+      "wait_timeout_knob": "the PUSH_WAIT_TIMEOUT_CYCLES build knob (frozen_build_knobs; frozen table and code default 0 = untimed, the shipped program text).  A positive value is a build-time switch for diagnostic builds only: local_pack then polls ld.relaxed.sys.u32 and traps the context (trap;) when the flag has not arrived within that many clock64 cycles.  The exported manifest records the built value.",
+      "inbox_read_rule": "local_pack reads ids / weights / row chunks / scale bytes of the slot through explicit coherent ld.global instructions (ld.global.b32 / ld.global.v4.b32 / ld.global.u8; never the non-coherent read-only ld.global.nc path, whose observation of the peers' released writes is not guaranteed by the PTX memory model), and its local push_inbox / push_flags pointers are declared without __restrict__ (plain uint8_t* / unsigned int*: peers write them while the kernel runs).",
+      "initialization_rule": "push_flags and push_generation are zero-initialized exactly once, at allocation, on every rank, and the host never writes them afterwards.  That zeroing (and the symmetric mapping of push_inbox / push_flags) must be complete and visible on EVERY rank before ANY rank's first publish_push: a collective rendezvous after allocation (device synchronize, then a process-group barrier) is required, which the in-tree runtime and the FlashInfer workspace allocation perform.  A rank that pushed into a destination whose flags were zeroed afterwards would lose that forward's flag.",
+      "peer_table_rule": "push_inbox_peers / push_flags_peers / pg_flags are by-value CakePeerPointerTable<T, 32> aggregates (capacity 32 pointer slots; entries [0, pg_world) = 16 are used, the rest are ignored); entry r is rank r's base pointer of the same symmetric buffer.  Self-entry equality: on every rank the table's own entry IS the local pointer bound beside it, push_inbox_peers[pg_rank] == push_inbox and push_flags_peers[pg_rank] == push_flags (publish_push and local_pack): local_pack polls its flags and reads its inbox through the local pointers while the sources write them through the tables, so a mismatch is a silent hang.  The generated reference bindings check it per launch with TVM_FFI_CHECK; the workspace must assert it once at allocation (pg_flags has no local pointer: no self-entry check).",
+      "local_pack_scalar_rule": "local_pack scalars: tokens_per_rank = this forward's token count (identical on every rank, <= 64); active_rows_per_expert = 32 (the SwapAB route tile; routes at or beyond it are counted in overflow[0]); scale_tile_k128 = 1 (the exported fc1 reads the K128 SFA tile layout, fc1_k128_tiles = 24; 0 selects the K256 layout no exported program reads).  The exported fc1 / fc2 programs fix the last two values; a routing-generic host passes them as constants.",
