+      "counter_layout": "fc2_completion is a symmetric u32[2] every rank owns (8 bytes, zero-initialized once at allocation): word 0 (fc2_done) receives one +1 from EVERY rank per forward (monotonic, 16 per forward, never reset); word 1 (fc2_arrivals) is the rank-LOCAL CTA arrival counter of one fc2 grid (returns to 0 at the end of every forward; peers never touch it).  Bound to fc2 as the plain local pointer fc2_completion (no __restrict__) + by-value CakePeerPointerTable<unsigned int, 32> fc2_completion_peers (entries [0, 16) used; entry r = rank r's base pointer), and to combine as the same pointer + table.  Self-entry equality: on every rank the table's own entry IS the local pointer, fc2_completion_peers[remote_pg_rank] == fc2_completion (fc2) and fc2_completion_peers[pg_rank] == fc2_completion (combine), the same way remote_terms_peers[remote_pg_rank] == remote_terms (fc2): fc2 counts arrivals and resets word 1 through the local pointer but sends its own +1 through the table, and combine polls word 0 through the local pointer, so a mismatch is a silent hang.  The generated reference bindings check it per launch with TVM_FFI_CHECK; the workspace must assert it once at allocation.",
+      "signal_rule": "each fc2 CTA, in its epilogue warps after its last tile: bar.sync 15, 128 (every remote route store of the CTA, a generic st.global.v4 through the peer pointer, happens-before the arrival; the terms are not async-proxy writes, so no bulk wait and no fence.proxy.async is involved); lane 0 of epilogue warp 0 atom.acq_rel.gpu.global.add.u32 +1 on fc2_completion[1]; the last arriver (old + 1 == gridDim.x) stores fc2_completion[1] = 0; the verdict is broadcast to the warp (shfl.sync) and ordered by bar.warp.sync; then the warp issues ONE red.release.sys.global.add.u32 +1 in which lane d < pg_world targets fc2_completion[0] of rank d through the peer table (itself included): 16 adds in one warp-wide instruction.  No separate fence.release.sys precedes the reduction: its .release qualifier is the signal's one system-scope release, cumulative (PTX memory model) over lane 0's acquire and so over every CTA's route stores.  Exactly one system fence (red.release.sys lowers to one MEMBAR.ALL.SYS + one REDG) and 16 remote adds per rank per forward; nothing per tile or per route, no per-add fence (a one-thread loop would serialise 16 system fences) and no explicit fence in front of the reduction (a second MEMBAR.ALL.SYS that drains nothing new).",
